2.3.1 General Ledger Enquiry
There are 4 Main Enquiry screen
    1. GLCC Balance Enquiry.
    a. GLCC (Optional) User can directly input GLCC. Or user can provide values individually. 
    b. Input Details: Branch Code or Name, Currency and CGL using the search and select from drop-down menus.
    c. User can use Reset button to clear all selection to default page.
    d. Date Range: Select from drop down.  In case of Custom Range user need to select/enter From Date and To Date.
    e. Search: Fill in all mandatory fields to enable the Search button and generate data.
    f. View Results: The application will display the required data if available, or show message “No balance records available for the selected criteria”.
    g. Export: Click the Export button to save the data as an Excel file.
    h. Sample Excel report.



    2. GLCC Transaction Enquiry
    a. GLCC (Optional) User can directly input GLCC. Or user can provide values individually. 
    b. Enter Details: Input Details: Branch Code or Name, Currency, CGL and Transaction Type (Default All Selection) using the search and drop-down menus.
    c. User can use Reset button to clear all selection to default page.
    d. Date Range: Select from drop down. In case of Custom Range user need to select/enter From Date and To Date.
    e. Additionally filter From Amount and To Amount (In Case user required specific amount range) this optional.
    f. Search: Fill in all mandatory fields to enable the Search button and generate data.
    g. View Results: The application will display the required data if available, or show message “No transactions available for the selected criteria”
    h. Export: Click the Export button to save the data as an Excel file. 

    3. GL Account Enquiry
    a. Enter Details: Select Circles (Default All Circles), Select Branches (Default All Branches), CGL, Currency (Default All Currencies) and Transaction Type (Default All Transaction Types) using the search and drop-down menus.
    b. User can use Reset button to clear all selection to default page.
    c. Date Range: Select from drop down. In case of Custom Range user need to select/enter From Date and To Date.
    d. User can use Reset button to clear all selection including default branch. Reset button will set Transaction Type, Select Circle and Currency to Default option.
    e. Search: Fill in all mandatory fields to enable the Search button and generate data.
    f. View Results: The application will display the required data if available, or show message “No transactions available for the selected criteria”
    g. Table filtering to be enabled for data visible on the screen.
    h. Export: Click the Export button to save the data as an Excel file. 
    i. Sample Excel report




    4. GL Balance Enquiry
    a. Enter Details: Select Circles (Default All Circles), Select Branches (Default All Branches in case of Collation), CGL (Default All CGLs), Currency (Default All Currencies) using the search and drop-down menus. Default Enquiry Type is Collation.
    b. In case of Enquiry Type is Consolidation then user can have Select Circle option (Select Branches will not be available).
    c. User can use Reset button to clear all selection and set to default.
    d. Balance Date: User can select single date for Collation or Consolidation data.
    e. Search: Fill in all mandatory fields to enable the Search button and generate data.
    f. View Results: The application will display the required data if available, or show message “No balances available for the selected criteria”
    g. Table filtering to be enabled for data visible on the screen.
    h. Export: Click the Export button to save the data as an Excel file. 
    i. Sample Excel report




